Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:49:57 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] solidcore-cadir: read a STEP edge without a parameter
 range

cadmpeg's neutral model bounds a STEP file's edges by their vertices alone, so an edge can
carry a curve with no parameter range. Upstream's CADIR reader refuses it. Port PR 16906's
fallback onto it: Assembly::add_edge_on finds the interval where the two vertices lie on the
curve, with topology::record_edge covering lines, conics, splines and polylines (a closed
spline restarted at its vertex), and the cadir reader calls it for such an edge.
